# Force LF for shell scripts regardless of core.autocrlf - the Maven Wrapper scripts (mvnw) run
# both on the host (Git Bash) and inside Linux Docker build stages (backend/*/Dockerfile). A
# CRLF-terminated mvnw breaks with "not found" inside a Linux container (bad shebang line) - hit
# for real building 4 of the 5 services' Docker images on Windows before this file existed.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf
mvnw.cmd text eol=crlf

# SQL is read by tools running inside Linux containers too - Flyway migrations and the
# backend/oracle-init/ user-creation script mounted into the gvenzl/oracle-free container.
# Keep LF so a CRLF checkout on Windows can't trip sqlplus / Flyway parsing.
*.sql text eol=lf
